  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi></math> slides over a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> on a horizontal surface. If the co-efficient of friction between the surfaces is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math> , then the work done against friction (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>) is:",
